# Synthesise Arlet Ottens' verilog-6502 to a flat gate-level netlist plus plain
# positive-edge D flip-flops.
#
# Run from the project root:  yowasp-yosys -s synth/synth_6502.ys
#
# NOTE: ABC (Yosys' logic optimiser / technology mapper) silently crashes in the
# yowasp-yosys WebAssembly build on this machine (0.70 and 0.71), so this flow
# uses -noabc. Output cells are $_AND_/$_OR_/$_XOR_/$_NOT_/$_MUX_ (and friends);
# src/netlist.py expands them into the CGP gate set. The result is correct but
# less optimised than an ABC-mapped netlist.

read_verilog vendor/verilog-6502/ALU.v vendor/verilog-6502/cpu.v
synth -top cpu -flatten -noabc

# The state register has an async reset; make it synchronous so every
# flip-flop is a plain D flip-flop (reset is held for several cycles anyway).
async2sync
# Turn enable / sync-reset flip-flops into plain DFFs with logic in front.
dfflegalize -cell $_DFF_P_ 01
techmap
opt -full -nodffe -nosdff
opt_clean -purge

tee -o build/cpu_gates.stat stat
write_json build/cpu_gates.json
